# Canonical SwiftFormat (nicklockwood/SwiftFormat) config for all emotiveapps
# Swift projects. SwiftFormat has no remote-include mechanism, so copy this
# file into each repo's root (or point at it with `swiftformat --config`).
#
# Kept deliberately non-conflicting with .swiftlint.yml in this repo, so that
# `swiftformat .` and `swiftlint --fix` never undo each other's work:
#   - trailingCommas enabled, SwiftLint's trailing_comma disabled: commas are
#     kept, so adding an item to a multiline list touches one line.
#   - maxwidth 140 matches SwiftLint's line_length warning.
#   - wrapMultilineStatementBraces disabled: pairs with SwiftLint's disabled
#     opening_brace rule (we wrap long signatures freely).
#   - decimalgrouping 3,6 matches SwiftLint number_separator minimum_length 6.
#   - trimwhitespace agrees with SwiftLint trailing_whitespace.
#   - wrap-arguments before-first with allow-partial-wrapping false does what
#     SwiftLint's multiline_arguments checks: once a call's arguments wrap, each
#     goes on its own line. wrap-parameters stays preserve, because it would
#     otherwise inherit before-first and rewrap declarations too.
--swiftversion 6.2
--allman false
--maxwidth 140
--disable redundantSelf,redundantStaticSelf,wrapMultilineStatementBraces,redundantReturn,andOperator
--decimalgrouping 3,6
--indent 2
--trimwhitespace always
--wrap-arguments before-first
--wrap-parameters preserve
--allow-partial-wrapping false
